        "answer": {
          "short": "$5$",
          "worked": "The reference angle is $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ and $\\frac{5\\pi}{4}$ is in quadrant III.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cot\\frac{5\\pi}{4}&=1\\\\\\sec\\frac{5\\pi}{4}&=-\\sqrt{2}\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}\\frac{5\\pi}{4}&=-\\sqrt{2}\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cot^2\\frac{5\\pi}{4}+\\sec^2\\frac{5\\pi}{4}+\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\frac{5\\pi}{4}&=1^2+(-\\sqrt{2})^2+(-\\sqrt{2})^2\\\\\\cot^2\\frac{5\\pi}{4}+\\sec^2\\frac{5\\pi}{4}+\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\frac{5\\pi}{4}&=5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
